            {
              "text": "For parenting arrangements, child custody disputes, and **accredited Family Dispute Resolution (FDR)** in **Ipswich, Queensland**, the best family law firms offer both child-focused advocacy and accredited practitioners (FDRPs) capable of issuing **Section 60I Certificates** if court action becomes necessary.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Richard Zande & Associates\n* **Location:** Central Ipswich (Limestone St)\n* **Strengths:** One of Ipswich’s longest-standing legal practices (over 60 years in the region). \n* **Dispute Resolution & Parenting:** They have accredited in-house **Family Dispute Resolution Practitioners (FDRPs)** who can mediate parenting plans and issue **Section 60I certificates** under the *Family Law Act 1975*. They handle everything from amicable consent orders to high-conflict custody disputes.\n\n### 2. Keane Legal\n* **Location:** Ipswich & Brookwater\n* **Strengths:** Strong focus on modern, out-of-court dispute resolution with transparent fixed-fee packages for parenting and custody issues.\n* **Dispute Resolution & Parenting:** They have qualified FDR mediators who conduct independent parenting mediations, facilitate shuttle conferences, and assist parents with drafting legally enforceable consent orders. They also provide independent legal representation if you already have an external mediator.\n\n### 3. Millwater Tyrrell Law (Sunshine Mediations)\n* **Location:** Heritage “Settler's Inn” Building, Brisbane Rd, Ipswich\n* **Strengths:** A well-regarded Ipswich firm run by local family lawyers David Millwater and Matthew Tyrrell. \n* **Dispute Resolution & Parenting:** They operate a dedicated mediation division, **Sunshine Mediations**, run by David Millwater. It offers cost-effective, private family mediation for parents looking to settle arrangements outside the court system.\n\n### 4. Best Wilson Buckley Family Law (BWB)\n* **Location:** Ipswich CBD (plus Brisbane & Toowoomba)\n* **Strengths:** Widely regarded as one of South East Queensland’s premier specialist family law firms, consisting entirely of dedicated family lawyers and accredited specialists.\n* **Dispute Resolution & Parenting:** Highly experienced in complex parenting arrangements, including relocation matters, parental alienation allegations, risk/harm assessments, and high-conflict custody disputes. They have senior lawyers trained in mediation and collaborative practice.\n\n### 5. Fallu McMillan Lawyers\n* **Location:** Ipswich CBD\n* **Strengths:** One of Ipswich’s oldest local firms, offering Queensland Law Society (QLS) Accredited Specialists in Family Law.\n* **Dispute Resolution & Parenting:** Ideal if your parenting dispute is high-conflict, involves family violence/DVOs, or requires formal legal advocacy during lawyer-assisted dispute resolution.\n\n---\n\n### Important Consideration: Mediator vs. Legal Representative\nUnder Australian family law:\n* **If you hire an Accredited FDRP as a mediator:** They must remain strictly neutral and cannot give either parent legal advice.\n* **If you want a lawyer to protect your interests:** You should hire a family lawyer to represent you *at* mediation (lawyer-assisted FDR) or to advise you before signing a parenting plan or consent orders.\n\n*If cost is a primary concern, you can also explore community-subsidised FDR services through **Relationships Australia (Ipswich branch)** or **Legal Aid Queensland (Ipswich Office)**.*",
